<div type="commentary"> 		
	<p>See <bibl><ptr target="bib:ARIE1937-1938"/></bibl> (p. 87): <quote>The last Pallava king Aparājita is represented by a single inscription
				(No. 165) from Tiruvoṟṟiyūr. It is dated in his 5th year and registers a gift of 30
				<foreign>kaḻañcu</foreign>s of gold by Kuṭṭiyāḷi Brahmādhirājaṉ 
				of Tirukkaṭavūr-nāṭu in Muṭṭukkūr-nāṭu,
				for a perpetual lamp to the god Mahādeva at Tiruvoṟṟiyūr. It is stated
				that the endowed amount was deposited with the <foreign>sabhā</foreign> of Maṇali, bearing interest at the rate of 3 <foreign>mañcāṭi</foreign>s per <foreign>kaḻañcu</foreign> per month, which works out at 15 per cent per annum.</quote></p>
</div>
      	
